    "label": {
      "en": "Employer old-age insurance contributions-whole income"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tscerpi_rate2"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "This is the employer old-age (pension) insurance contribution rate of 2.02% (2025 value; scheduled to rise to 2.11% under the 2026 rules), applied to the employee's whole gross income, in addition to the 8.55% rate charged on Income Group A only ($tscerpi_rate1). It is used in tscer_fr's BenCalc function (Comp_perTU parameter, 'Old-age insurance contributions-main') to compute the whole-income component of the employer's basic pension contribution, which is subject to the general reduction on employer contributions."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Reduction coefficient"
    },
